{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792484559,"nonce":"AVDLSXnV3RYxV1o9qbyK39D29m4=","message":"Frontend tables and sets now use FxHashMap/FxHashSet. Retained identities, readonly views, bindings and dependency-worklist entries use InternedString handles; stable source spellings are borrowed for ordered field metadata. A per-compilation cache interns each spelling once, avoiding repeated global-interner locks. Native function targets are cached, generated names reuse a formatting buffer, field lookup compares symbols without resolving strings, and borrowed binding lookup no longer clones metadata. Signatures use shared immutable Rc handles with exclusive finalization; the signature type does not implement Clone.\n\nCanonical layouts use a hash cache with a stack key for small shapes. Object literals reuse their source-ordered temporary values to construct sorted layouts, eliminating a separate field map and preserving initializer evaluation order. Return inference stores one candidate rather than allocating a vector per function. Existing ownership, layout, evaluation-order and conformance checks pass.\n\nReproduction: cargo test -p zyntax_ts --features allocation-audit --test allocations --offline -- --ignored --nocapture. The audit uses the compiler's CountingAllocator and a fixed 1,000-function annotated source with repeated two-field records. Before the allocation refactor (inference worklist present): cold 64,110 allocations, 4,442 reallocations, 16,277,784 requested bytes; warm 64,095 allocations, 4,418 reallocations, 15,933,620 requested bytes. After: cold 25,104 allocations, 42 reallocations, 12,472,281 requested bytes; warm 25,089 allocations, 18 reallocations, 12,111,735 requested bytes. These are local ARM64 Rust frontend heap-request counts, not native-library/slab/RSS measurements and not NUC throughput benchmarks. Shared TypeRegistry initialization and required typed AST nodes remain included in both arms.","files":null}]}